I've discovered that Valkyries suit my playing style. I don't know if
it's the instant Excalibur or what, but the last 3 Valkyries I've
played all had a decent shot at the castle.

Good game. AC -28. Blessed +6 Excalibur. Intrinsics out the wazoo
(including fire resistance, disint. resistance, teleport and teleport
control, etc etc). I walk up to the courtyard in front of the castle.
I'm carrying 9 wands, only one I haven't identifed. Zap it at the
door, nope, it's not the one I need. So, I walk next to the moat,
zap it again. Still doesn't work.

Decide "hmm, time to walk across some water" so I put on the -1 boots
of levitation I've been carrying since level 8 of the dungeon, for
JUST THIS PURPOSE. What happens? The eel grabs me and pulls me under
while I'm changing boots.

The weird thing is my final intrinsics included levitation - can an
eel drown you even if you're levitating? How obnoxious.

Also, I think there's a rather serious bug concerning invisibility
and monsters with missle attacks. If an Elf can't see me to walk up
and hit me with his lame little sword, how come that same Elf can
throw daggers at me and hit me?
